From 1795b0d4a9e1adbedca83cae8456ba9fef456dc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:21:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: panel: add the BOE TV101WUM-NM0

Describe the BOE module fitted to the Amazon Fire HD 10 (2017), an MT8173
tablet, as a third NT51021 panel.

The part number is not read off the module itself -- getting at its label
means removing the main board -- so it is worth setting out how it was
arrived at, since it rests on identifying the panel this board second-
sources against.

The vendor firmware picks between a BOE and an Innolux module from two
board ID straps, so whatever the two are, they are mechanically and
electrically interchangeable in one chassis. An Innolux module pulled from
one of these tablets carries "Innolux P101KDA-AB0" on its back, and that
part is 216.576 x 135.36 mm active, 227.926 x 143 x 4.4 mm outline, 51-pin
MIPI with four data lanes, a four-string WLED backlight and a 3.3 V supply.
The BOE second source therefore has to match that outline and connector.

Of BOE's 10.1" WUXGA family only TV101WUM-NM0 and its later sibling
TV101WUM-NM1 do: TV101WUM-NX0 is 45-pin on a 227.31 x 141.5 mm outline,
TV101WUM-NH0 is 39-pin, TV101WUM-NS0 is 34-pin, and TV101WUM-NH1, though
also 51-pin, is a 1.85 mm-thick module rather than 4.4 mm. Measured on the
board, this tablet's LCM flex is silkscreened 1 at one end and 51 at the
other, its active area is 216 x 135 mm, and its backlight regulator is
configured for four LED strings, all of which agree. NM0 is the earlier of
the two registrations and so the one contemporaneous with this device, and
a replacement-part listing for this model names it; NM1 is the same
mechanical design and would take the same programming.

So this is an identification rather than a reading, and the one thing it
settles outright is that the module is not the boe,tv101wum-nx0 above it: a
45-pin panel cannot be fitted to a chassis wired for a 51-pin flex.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/display/panel/novatek,nt51021.yaml      | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/novatek,nt51021.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/novatek,nt51021.yaml
index 550aefaea..0308f7745 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/novatek,nt51021.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/novatek,nt51021.yaml
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ description: |
   panels.
   Right now, support is added only for a BOE WUXGA LCD display panels with a
   resolution of 1200x1920. They are video mode DSI panels.
+  The TV101WUM-NM0 is fitted to the Amazon Fire HD 10 (2017).
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: panel-common.yaml#
@@ -22,6 +23,7 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     items:
       - enum:
+          - boe,tv101wum-nm0
           - boe,tv101wum-nx0
           - boe,tv080wum-nx2
       - const: novatek,nt51021
